{"phase":"post","id":"toolu_01QhGk4W8DMMZgqRCFhCAjpf","tool":"WebSearch","result":"{\"query\":\"\\\"Instar 2.0\\\" agent AI\",\"results\":[{\"tool_use_id\":\"srvtoolu_01HMZnWj8YikXC6ibcLzy4oS\",\"content\":[{\"title\":\"Sierra Agent OS 2.0: from answers to memory and action\",\"url\":\"https://sierra.ai/blog/agent-os-2-0\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - JKHeadley/instar: Persistent Claude Code agents with scheduling, sessions, memory, and Telegram. · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/JKHeadley/instar\"},{\"title\":\"instar - npm\",\"url\":\"https://www.npmjs.com/package/instar\"},{\"title\":\"feat(witness): v0 package — signed, offline-verifiable records of work between agents by JKHeadley · Pull Request #2161 · JKHeadley/instar\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/JKHeadley/instar/pull/2161\"},{\"title\":\"INSTAR: An Agent-Based Model that integrates existing knowledge to simulate the population dynamics of a forest pest - ScienceDirect\",\"url\":\"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0304380019302728\"},{\"title\":\"AI agent\",\"url\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/AI_agent\"},{\"title\":\"Instar — Claude Code, with a mind of its own\",\"url\":\"https://instar.sh/\"},{\"title\":\"AI fürs Smarthome - Scripts / Programmierung - INSTAR Forum\",\"url\":\"https://forum.instar.com/t/ai-fuers-smarthome/31313\"},{\"title\":\"I Built a Claude Code Agent That Doesn't Need Me Anymore\",\"url\":\"https://instar.sh/blog/why-i-built-instar\"}]},\"I found search results related to \\\"Instar\\\" and AI agents, though no specific result labeled exactly \\\"Instar 2.0\\\" appeared. Here's what's relevant:\\n\\n## Instar (AI Agent Project)\\nThe most relevant match is **Instar**, an open-source project for persistent AI agents. Instar is scaffolding designed to give AI agents coherence—it remembers past conversations, catches its own contradictions, follows through on commitments across restarts, and carries a self-improving loop. It runs on the Claude Code or Codex subscription, and is engine-agnostic, with local open-source models on the roadmap.\\n\\nKey details:\\n- Instar turns Claude Code from a powerful CLI tool into a coherent, autonomous partner, with persistent identity, shared values, memory that survives every restart, and the infrastructure to evolve.\\n- It has a self-evolving system that carries the same loop that built Instar itself—proposing, learning, and following through, evolving its capabilities and understanding over time.\\n- Instar was extracted from the Dawn/Portal project, a production AI system where a human and an AI have been building together for months, with infrastructure patterns earned through real experience and real failures.\\n\\n## Other unrelated \\\"Instar\\\" results:\\n- **Sierra Agent OS 2.0** — a different product (not \\\"Instar 2.0\\\") for building customer-facing AI agents, launched with features like Agent Studio 2.0 and Insights 2.0.\\n- **INSTAR (scientific model)** — an unrelated Agent-Based Model aiming to simulate the population dynamics of the Thaumetopoea pityocampa forest pest.\\n- **INSTAR cameras** — a German smart-home camera brand with AI object detection features, unrelated to AI agents in the software sense.\\n\\nI didn't find a specific release or announcement explicitly called \\\"Instar 2.0.\\\" If you're referring to a particular version update, let me know and I can search more specifically (e.g., \\\"Instar v2\\\" or a changelog/release note).\"],\"durationSeconds\":11.109512707999999,\"searchCount\":1}"}
{"phase":"post","id":"toolu_01LF1zYSiKwoADCXhpF3uRCG","tool":"WebSearch","result":"{\"query\":\"Hermes agent OpenClaw agent \\\"Meta Muse\\\" AI assistant 2026\",\"results\":[{\"tool_use_id\":\"srvtoolu_01LPh815tW9eqeZchutyfPr7\",\"content\":[{\"title\":\"Meta Muse vs OpenClaw: The Turnkey AI Agent\",\"url\":\"https://www.starkinsider.com/2026/09/meta-muse-vs-openclaw-personal-ai-agent.html\"},{\"title\":\"6 Best Open Source Meta Muse Alternatives in 2026\",\"url\":\"https://openalternative.co/alternatives/meta-muse\"},{\"title\":\"Always-On Agents: Dots vs Grok Bot vs Muse\",\"url\":\"https://aimultiple.com/always-on-agents\"},{\"title\":\"The 11 Best Personal AI Agents in 2026 - AGNT.gg\",\"url\":\"https://agnt.gg/articles/agents/best-personal-ai-agents\"},{\"title\":\"Meta Muse vs Hermes Agent: Trust, Model Choice, and Cost\",\"url\":\"https://lobsterland.ing/blog/openclaw-internals/meta-muse-vs-hermes-agent/\"},{\"title\":\"Muse vs Hermes Agent vs OpenClaw: who should run which\",\"url\":\"https://technspire.com/sv/blog/muse-vs-hermes-agent-vs-openclaw-who-should-run-which\"},{\"title\":\"Hermes Agent vs OpenClaw 2026: Full Comparison of Two Top AI Agents\",\"url\":\"https://www.explainx.ai/blog/hermes-agent-vs-openclaw-comparison-2026\"},{\"title\":\"Meta Muse vs OpenClaw Launch: AI Agents Compared (2026)\",\"url\":\"https://openclawlaunch.com/compare/muse\"},{\"title\":\"Meta Muse vs Hermes Agent: Two Different Kinds of AI Agent (2026)\",\"url\":\"https://openclawlaunch.com/guides/hermes-agent-meta-muse\"}]},\"Here's a summary of what the search results reveal about these three AI agent products in 2026:\\n\\n**Meta Muse**: Meta launched Muse on September 8, 2026, for adults in the US, and it has since reached Canada. It's Meta's personal agent that runs on a dedicated Muse Secure VM — a persistent, isolated Linux computer with its own browser that you and the agent share. It achieved rapid adoption — Meta's Muse passed 2.5 million downloads in its first 13 days, as reported by CNBC on 21 September. It's powered by a proprietary model, as Muse runs only on Meta's Muse Spark model.\\n\\n**OpenClaw**: This is a self-hosted AI agent framework that crossed 100,000 GitHub stars in its first week in January 2026, now at 387K+ (Aug 23, 2026), making it one of the fastest-growing projects in GitHub history. The OpenClaw Foundation, a US non-profit announced on July 8, maintains it. Notably, Reuters reported that Meta modeled Muse on OpenClaw.\\n\\n**Hermes Agent**: This is a cross-platform desktop agent from Nous Research that connects to Telegram, Discord, Slack, WhatsApp, and more, with persistent memory, scheduling, and isolated sandboxing, running natively on macOS, Windows, and Linux. Its distinguishing feature is persistence: the core idea is persistence — most agents start fresh every session, but Hermes maintains memory across conversations, auto-generates skills from past interactions, and builds up context about your projects over time, so you don't have to re-explain things.\\n\\n**Key architectural differences**: According to one comparison, Hermes Agent by Nous Research has 188k GitHub stars and is the self-improving runtime that writes its own skills, while OpenClaw by Peter Steinberger (now OpenClaw Foundation) has 247k GitHub stars, 24 supported messaging channels, and the largest skill ecosystem. The learning capability sets Hermes apart: Hermes Agent has a closed Curator learning loop — every 15 tool calls and after complex tasks, it reflects on what worked, writes a Markdown skill file, and improves on subsequent runs, whereas OpenClaw does not have a built-in learning loop, with its strength being the breadth of channels supported (24+) and the size of the ClawHub skill ecosystem (5,400+ claws).\\n\\nInterestingly, there's also crossover potential — Hermes Agent can import OpenClaw settings, memories and skills directly.\"],\"durationSeconds\":13.45955025,\"searchCount\":1}"}
