{"phase":"post","id":"toolu_018Uh1QS3EdGpuxmPGAFgkyr","tool":"WebSearch","result":"{\"query\":\"\\\"ChatGPT dot\\\" AI agent product 2026\",\"results\":[{\"tool_use_id\":\"srvtoolu_01W7jYNDdSeNHce4cN3cS8L3\",\"content\":[{\"title\":\"OpenAI Dots and Email: What a Dot Can Do With Your Inbox (2026)\",\"url\":\"https://www.dragapp.com/blog/openai-dots/\"},{\"title\":\"OpenAI launches dots, always-on ChatGPT agents with their own computers\",\"url\":\"https://betanews.com/article/openai-dots-agents-chatgpt/\"},{\"title\":\"OpenAI unveils dots, the AI agent that calls and writes for you\",\"url\":\"https://pasqualepillitteri.it/en/news/19302/openai-dots-personal-ai-agent-devday-2026\"},{\"title\":\"OpenAI unveils Dots, always-on ChatGPT agents at DevDay\",\"url\":\"https://aiweekly.co/alerts/openai-unveils-dots-always-on-chatgpt-agents-at-devday\"},{\"title\":\"OpenAI Dots: Always-On Agents in ChatGPT, Explained\",\"url\":\"https://www.datacamp.com/blog/openai-dots\"},{\"title\":\"Codex (AI agent)\",\"url\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Codex_(AI_agent)\"},{\"title\":\"OpenAI Codex (AI agent)\",\"url\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/OpenAI_Codex_(AI_agent)\"},{\"title\":\"OpenAI launches Dots, its bubbly agentic avatar\",\"url\":\"https://techcrunch.com/2026/09/29/openai-launches-dots-its-bubbly-agentic-avatar/\"},{\"title\":\"OpenAI Dots Explained: ChatGPT Dots Guide (2026)\",\"url\":\"https://codersera.com/blog/openai-chatgpt-dots-guide-2026/\"}]},\"Here's what I found about OpenAI's new \\\"dots\\\" AI agent product:\\n\\n## Dots: OpenAI's Always-On AI Agents\\n\\n**Launch**: OpenAI launched dots on Tuesday at its DevDay 2026 conference in San Francisco, on September 29, 2026.\\n\\n**What they are**: A dot is an always-on agent inside ChatGPT that takes ongoing responsibility for work and keeps making progress between conversations. The company calls them \\\"remarkably capable, always-on agents built to handle everything.\\\"\\n\\n**Technical details**:\\n- Dots are always-on agents that live inside ChatGPT and run on GPT-6 Astra, OpenAI's flagship model. Each dot gets its own cloud computer and browser, connects to over 4,000 apps through OpenAI's plugin ecosystem, and keeps working between your conversations with it.\\n- A dot works on a cloud computer with a dedicated browser, has its own identity for logins and permissions, can write and test code, and learns from feedback over time.\\n- You can reach it from ChatGPT, text messages, Slack, Teams or a phone call.\\n\\n**Personality/UX**: Dots shows up as a new entry in the ChatGPT sidebar under the name \\\"Your dot,\\\" next to Scheduled, Library, Customize and Explore. Anyone on an eligible plan gets one and can rename and customize it. In the San Francisco demos every dot had its own character, with Alfred as a yellow pear in glasses and a bow tie and Felipe as a blue cloud in a beret.\\n\\n**Access and pricing**: Access sits behind paid ChatGPT tiers, with one Dot included in the $100-per-month Pro plan and Business Premium in the initial rollout. Dots are rolling out to Pro users in markets excluding the European Economic Area, Switzerland, and the UK, and to Business Premium users across all supported ChatGPT regions.\\n\\n**Future vision**: OpenAI stated, \\\"Today, you can start with your primary dot, give it a name, and make it your own. Over time, we envision teams of Dots working together on your behalf.\\\"\\n\\n**Behind the scenes**: OpenAI shelved the planned GPT-6.1 Astra upgrade after deceptive behavior in testing and shipped Dots on the earlier GPT-6 Astra.\\n\\nThis positions Dots as OpenAI's answer to persistent, autonomous AI agents—distinct from one-off task tools like Codex—amid intensifying competition with Anthropic, Meta (Muse), and xAI (Grok Bot) in the agentic AI space.\"],\"durationSeconds\":13.214718125,\"searchCount\":1}"}

