{"phase":"post","id":"toolu_01R7z53fmJ5LA61PzvPFSnKk","tool":"WebSearch","result":"{\"query\":\"ChatGPT \\\"Dot\\\" feature OR product 2026\",\"results\":[{\"tool_use_id\":\"srvtoolu_01DADNVSqSLPzb6Lt6wcRBbk\",\"content\":[{\"title\":\"OpenAI launches Dots that keep working without user prompts\",\"url\":\"https://www.medianama.com/2026/10/223-openai-launches-dots-devday-2026/\"},{\"title\":\"OpenAI Dots and Email: What a Dot Can Do With Your Inbox (2026)\",\"url\":\"https://www.dragapp.com/blog/openai-dots/\"},{\"title\":\"ChatGPT\",\"url\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/ChatGPT\"},{\"title\":\"OpenAI Dots: Always-On ChatGPT Agents Explained\",\"url\":\"https://www.relevantaudience.com/ai/openai-dots-always-on-agents-chatgpt/\"},{\"title\":\"OpenAI Dots Explained: ChatGPT Dots Guide (2026)\",\"url\":\"https://codersera.com/blog/openai-chatgpt-dots-guide-2026/\"},{\"title\":\"A Guide to ChatGPT Dots: How OpenAI's Always-On Agents Work\",\"url\":\"https://composio.dev/content/a-guide-to-chatgpt-dots-how-openai-s-always-on-agents-work\"},{\"title\":\"OpenAI Dots: Always-On Agents in ChatGPT, Explained\",\"url\":\"https://www.datacamp.com/blog/openai-dots\"},{\"title\":\"ChatGPT Updates by OpenAI - October 2026 - Releasebot\",\"url\":\"https://releasebot.io/updates/openai/chatgpt\"},{\"title\":\"ChatGPT Atlas\",\"url\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/ChatGPT_Atlas\"}]},\"Here's what I found on OpenAI's \\\"Dots\\\" feature in ChatGPT:\\n\\n## What are ChatGPT Dots?\\n\\nAt DevDay 2026, OpenAI introduced dots: persistent AI agents powered by GPT-6 Astra, that operate independently in the cloud and continue tasks without user prompts. OpenAI launched dots on 29 September 2026: always-on agents in ChatGPT, powered by GPT-6 Astra, that each run on their own cloud computer and keep working toward a user's goals 24/7.\\n\\n## Key Capabilities\\n- Each dot runs on GPT-6 Astra with its own cloud computer and browser, and OpenAI says it can connect to over 4,000 apps through plugins.\\n- A dot is a named, avatar-style agent inside ChatGPT that takes ongoing responsibility for work you hand it and keeps making progress when you are not talking to it — researching in the background, running scheduled jobs like a daily calendar review, messaging you in Slack when it needs a decision, and handing coding work to Codex.\\n- A dot can monitor customer feedback, implement and test minor fixes, and submit pull requests with video documentation.\\n- They are powered by GPT-6 Astra, and you control them with Custom Rules that decide which actions need your approval.\\n\\n## Availability and Pricing\\n- At launch, dots are available on ChatGPT Pro outside the EEA, Switzerland and the UK, on Business Premium in all supported regions, and in beta on Enterprise, Edu and Healthcare once an admin turns them on.\\n- Dots are not free: your first dot is included with ChatGPT Pro (from $100/month) or Business Premium, and you must be 18+.\\n- The first dot is included in Pro and Business Premium at no extra cost, and conversations with it do not count toward ChatGPT usage limits.\\n- As for future pricing, OpenAI says users will later be able to add more dots and scale each one by speed or monthly workload.\\n\\n## Setup\\nYou create your first dot in the ChatGPT desktop app or ChatGPT on desktop web, follow the onboarding prompts, connect your apps, and let it introduce itself.\\n\\n## How It Differs from Previous ChatGPT Agent Features\\nEarlier ChatGPT agent features ran a task when you asked, then stopped. In contrast, a dot is persistent — it's not just ChatGPT that keeps running after you close the window; the bigger change is persistent responsibility.\\n\\nThis appears to be a genuinely new, very recently launched (late September/early October 2026) feature rather than something from my existing knowledge base, so this search was necessary to provide accurate, current details.\"],\"durationSeconds\":10.460028875,\"searchCount\":1}"}
